        </article>
    

          </section>
        
          <input type="radio" name="selectedTabId" id="release-f34959dc65fa6147308490ca57154086"  />
          <label for="release-f34959dc65fa6147308490ca57154086">
            At a Glance
          </label>
          <section class="presskit-section--white" aria-labelledby="release-f34959dc65fa6147308490ca57154086" role="tabpanel">
            <div class="release__in-brief d-block d-md-none">
              
            </div>
            






































    

        <h2 class="release-banner__title" >
            At a Glance: 2023 Nissan Z
        </h2>

        
        

        <article id="release-f34959dc65fa6147308490ca57154086">
            

            

            <div id="overview" class="row">
                <div class="col-12">
                    <div id="releaseBody" class="row">
                        <div class="col-12">
                            <p class="publication">
                                
                                    <date class="published-at published published-show">

        <time class="pub-date" datetime="2021-08-18T00:00:00Z">
          August 18, 2021
        </time>
      
</date>

                                    
                                
                            </p>

                            <div class="release__in-brief d-block d-md-none">
                              
                            </div>

                            <w-release>
                                <p>In 1969, a revolutionary Japanese two-door sports car made its U.S. debut in New York City &ndash; the Datsun 240Z. In 2021, an all-new, just as revolutionary, seventh-generation version makes its global debut also in New York. This time, the nameplate simply reads "Z."</p>
<p>From a design standpoint, the all-new 2023 Z offers a sleek, attractive exterior with a silhouette that shows respect for the original model &ndash; with a long hood and low rear stance. Inside, the driver-centric cockpit includes a 12.3-inch customizable racing-inspired TFT meter display, available leather-appointed sports seats and 8-speaker Bose&reg; Audio system.</p>
<p>All 2023 Nissan Z models are equipped with a 400-horsepower 3.0-liter V6 twin turbo engine and choice of 6-speed manual transmission with motorsports-inspired EXEDY&reg; high-performance clutch, or a 9-speed automatic transmission with aluminum paddle shifters.</p>
<p>The 2023 Z is offered in Sport and Performance grade levels and a special Proto Spec edition, which is limited to 240 units.</p>
<p>Highlights of the 2023 Nissan Z include:</p>
<p><strong>Body:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Traditional rear-wheel drive sports car design with high rigidity body, commanding presence and advanced aerodynamics</li>
<li>Long hood, lower rear stance</li>
<li>Heritage-style LED headlights and LED daytime running lights</li>
<li>Rear LED combination lights</li>
<li>Lightweight aluminum hood, doors and hatchback</li>
<li>Dual body-colored power outside mirrors with integrated LED turn signals</li>
<li>Side sill spoilers, available front chin spoiler and rear spoiler (Performance)</li>
<li>Six available two-tone premium exterior color schemes, each featuring a Super Black roof and choice of: Brilliant Silver, Boulder Gray, Seiran Blue, Ikazuchi Yellow, Passion Red TriCoat and Everest White Pearl TriCoat</li>
<li>Three available monotone exterior colors: Black Diamond Metallic, Gun Metallic and Rosewood Metallic</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Engine and Driveline</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Front engine/rear-wheel drive</li>
<li>VR30DDTT 3.0L V6 Twin Turbo engine, 24-valve DOHC V6 rated at 400 horsepower @ 6,400 RPM, 350 lb-ft of torque @ 1,600 &ndash; 5,200 RPM</li>
<li>Electronic Variable Valve Timing Control (E-VVT)</li>
<li>Micro-finished crankshaft and camshaft; small pitch, silent cam chain; drive-by-wire throttle</li>
<li>Oil cooler, electric cooling fan</li>
<li>Standard 6-speed close-ratio manual transmission with EXEDY&reg; high-performance clutch</li>
<li>Available SynchroRev Match&reg;, allowing heel-toe-like downshifting (manual transmission)</li>
<li>Available electronically controlled 9-speed automatic transmission with manual shift mode, launch control, Downshift Rev Matching</li>
<li>Motorsports-inspired EXEDY&reg; high-performance clutch (manual transmission models)</li>
<li>Standard aluminum paddle shifters (Sport 9AT); available unique GT‑R design paddle shifters (Performance 9AT)</li>
<li>Dual outlet exhaust, available sport grade muffler (Performance)</li>
<li>Carbon fiber composite driveshaft (6MT)</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Suspension, Steering and Braking</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Double-wishbone front suspension, rear multi-link suspension; 2-point front strut tower brace; high response monotube shock absorbers</li>
<li>Large diameter front and rear hollow stabilizer bars</li>
<li>Available sport-tuned suspension (Performance)</li>
<li>Vehicle speed-sensitive electric power steering (electric rack)</li>
<li>Available mechanical clutch-type limited-slip differential (Performance)</li>
<li>Power-assisted vented front and rear disc brakes, 4-wheel anti-lock braking system with electronic brake force distribution and brake assist</li>
<li>Available Nissan Sport Brakes with 14.0-inch front/13.8-inch rear rotors and 4-piston front/2-piston rear aluminum calipers, red caliper finish (Performance)</li>
<li>Available yellow painted brake calipers (Proto Spec)</li>
<li>18-inch aluminum-alloy wheels and 245/45R18 front / 245/45R18 rear Yokohama ADVAN Sport high performance tires</li>
<li>Available 19-inch RAYS&reg; super-lightweight forged-alloy wheels with 255/40R19 front / 275/35R19 rear Bridgestone Potenza&reg; S007 high performance tires (Performance)<strong><u></u></strong></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Interior Features</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>2-passenger seating, designed to fit driver and passenger like a glove</li>
<li>Seamlessly blends modern technology with classic Z hallmarks</li>
<li>240Z-inspired center stack with instrument panel-mounted analog triple-pod cluster (turbocharger boost, turbocharger turbine speed, voltmeter)</li>
<li>8-way manual driver's seat, 4-way manual passenger's seat</li>
<li>Available 4-way power adjustable driver's seat with manual lifter, lumbar and thigh support; 4-way power passenger seat (Performance)</li>
<li>Heated seats (Performance)</li>
<li>Black woven seat cloth with synthetic suede inserts</li>
<li>Available leather-appointed seating surfaces with synthetic suede inserts (Performance)</li>
<li>Automatic Temperature Control</li>
<li>Leather-wrapped 3-spoke steering wheel</li>
<li>Standard 8.0-inch display audio touchscreen with 6-speaker audio system</li>
<li>Available 9.0-inch touchscreen with navigation (Performance)<strong><u></u></strong></li>
<li>Available Bose&reg; audio system with 8 speakers (Performance)</li>
<li>Available Active Noise Cancellation (Performance)</li>
<li>Available Active Sound Enhancement (Performance)</li>
<li>SiriusXM&reg; Radio (SiriusXM&reg; subscription required, sold separately)</li>
<li>Bluetooth&reg; Hands-free Phone System</li>
<li>Hands-free Text Messaging Assistant</li>
<li>Available NissanConnect&reg; Services powered by SiriusXM</li>
<li>Available NissanConnect&reg; with WiFi</li>
<li>Voice Recognition</li>
<li>RearView Monitor <strong><u></u></strong></li>
<li>Streaming Audio via Bluetooth&reg; <strong><u></u></strong></li>
<li>Available aluminum-trimmed pedals (Performance)</li>
<li>Available HomeLink&reg; Universal Transceiver (Performance)</li>
<li>Two 12-volt power outlets</li>
<li>Two USB ports (1 Type-A, 1 Type C)</li>
<li>Intelligent Cruise Control (Full Speed Range)</li>
<li>Nissan Intelligent Key&reg; with Push Button Ignition<strong><u></u></strong></li>
<li>Front and rear parking sensors<strong><u></u></strong></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Safety, Security and Driving Assistance Technologies</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Seat-mounted side impact supplemental air bags</li>
<li>Roof-mounted curtain side-impact supplemental air bags</li>
<li>Vehicle Security System</li>
<li>Vehicle Dynamic Control with Traction Control System</li>
<li>Tire Pressure Monitoring System</li>
<li>Automatic Emergency Braking with Pedestrian Detection</li>
<li>Blind Spot Warning</li>
<li>Lane Departure Warning</li>
<li>Rear Cross Traffic Alert</li>
<li>Intelligent Forward Collision Warning</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Models</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Offered in two models: Z Sport and Z Performance</li>
<li>One available option: Proto Spec (Performance model only) with yellow-colored brake calipers, bronze-colored 19-inch RAYS aluminum-alloy wheels, exclusive shift lever knob (MT only), exclusive Proto Spec leather-appointed seats with yellow accents, exclusive Proto Spec suede + cloth door trim with yellow stitching, special Proto Spec interior stitching</li>
</ul>
<p align="center"># # #</p>
                            </w-release>

                        </div>
                    </div>

                    

                    
